  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Ten students sit a test consisting of twenty questions. Two students get eight questions correct and one student gets nine questions correct. The remaining seven students all get at least ten questions correct and the average number of questions answered correctly by these seven students is an integer. If the average number of questions answered correctly by all ten students is also an integer, then find that integer.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p27-q15-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "13 questions.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-q15-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The seven students must average 15 for the overall average to be an integer.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $k$ be the integer average for the remaining seven students. Since each answers between 10 and 20 questions correctly, $10\\le k\\le20$. Their total score is $7k$.\n\nThe overall average is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{8+8+9+7k}{10}&=\\frac{25+7k}{10}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor this to be an integer, $25+7k$ must be divisible by 10. Hence $7k$ must end in 5, so $k$ must end in 5. The only such integer between 10 and 20 is $k=15$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{25+7(15)}{10}&=\\frac{130}{10}\\\\\\frac{25+7(15)}{10}&=13.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, the average for all ten students is 13 questions.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 78
  },
